WEBVTT

00:04.052 --> 00:06.095
BUDOGAOKA BANK

00:08.056 --> 00:12.435
GREAT YEAR-END LOTTERY

00:09.516 --> 00:12.268
Please accept our congratulations
on this momentous occasion.

00:12.727 --> 00:16.939
It is very, very close to expiring,
but there is no question,

00:17.023 --> 00:20.693
this is the third-place ticket
worth five million yen.

00:21.403 --> 00:23.947
Now, then… If I may…

00:24.239 --> 00:27.450
This is a promissory note
for the award of five million yen.

00:27.367 --> 00:29.118
MORIOH STATION BRANCH

00:28.285 --> 00:29.140
Please allow us three days
to process

00:31.162 --> 00:33.747
before collecting your cash reward.

00:34.833 --> 00:36.125
PROMISSORY NOTE
BUDOGAOKA BANK
MORIOH STATION BRANCH
TOTAL 5,000,000 YEN
PLEASE PAY THE AMOUNT STATED
ABOVE IN EXCHANGE FOR
THIS PROMISSORY NOTE.

00:37.419 --> 00:40.713
One, ten, hundred, thousand…

00:41.089 --> 00:43.091
It's got six zeros…

01:08.658 --> 01:09.283
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE
DIAMOND IS UNBREAKABLE

01:09.367 --> 01:11.494
<i>A demon's crept into
our everyday life</i>

01:11.578 --> 01:13.871
<i>It's about to take away
something precious</i>

01:13.955 --> 01:17.166
<i>Our peace has already
crumbled long ago</i>

01:17.959 --> 01:20.044
<i>So casually, so nonchalantly</i>

01:20.128 --> 01:22.421
<i>It's taken from us
before we know it</i>

01:22.505 --> 01:25.758
<i>If we want it back,
now's the chance</i>

01:25.967 --> 01:29.512
<i>With the sharpness of
the piercing arrow</i>

01:30.305 --> 01:33.683
<i>The beauty of two souls united</i>

01:33.767 --> 01:36.352
<i>Wherever you go, chase you</i>

01:36.436 --> 01:38.563
<i>Whenever, chase you</i>

01:38.646 --> 01:40.606
<i>I will chase you</i>

01:40.690 --> 01:42.316
<i>Nowhere to escape</i>

01:42.400 --> 01:44.944
<i>Start running, I will chase you</i>

01:45.028 --> 01:47.071
<i>Tomorrow, chase you</i>

01:47.155 --> 01:49.866
<i>My fists will be the one
to show you</i>

01:50.033 --> 01:54.533
<i>Tenacity decides
who will win or lose</i>

01:55.747 --> 02:00.247
<i>So I chase you</i>

02:03.421 --> 02:05.548
EPISODE 19
SHIGECHI'S HARVEST, PART 2

02:03.963 --> 02:08.051
Now, there is something
I would like to ask you…

02:05.632 --> 02:08.051
RECEPTION

02:09.511 --> 02:14.011
From which store did you sirs
procure this winning ticket?

02:15.934 --> 02:17.018
Sniff, sniff.

02:17.102 --> 02:18.436
W-Which store?

02:19.896 --> 02:23.399
Now why would you wanna know that?

02:23.817 --> 02:27.195
It's a simple formality.

02:28.488 --> 02:30.573
<i>Damn dim-witted hoodlums.</i>

02:30.698 --> 02:33.742
<i>You won five million yen? Bullshit.</i>

02:34.077 --> 02:38.372
<i>This quick-witted teller
smells foul play.</i>

02:38.748 --> 02:40.583
Or perhaps

02:40.667 --> 02:43.336
I am sensing some resistance
to answering my question?

02:43.545 --> 02:47.465
W-Well, of course we bought it
in Morioh.

02:47.715 --> 02:50.926
Oh? How very peculiar…

02:51.094 --> 02:55.594
Not a single store
in Morioh sells lottery tickets.

03:03.356 --> 03:05.524
O-Oh, right…

03:06.192 --> 03:09.945
It must've been when
we went to S City.

03:10.321 --> 03:13.949
We bought so much stuff,
it must've just slipped my mind…

03:14.075 --> 03:16.952
I-I-I-I-I-It was so long ago…

03:20.081 --> 03:23.667
I just noticed
something else peculiar…

03:24.669 --> 03:27.088
On the reverse side of the ticket,

03:27.338 --> 03:29.673
you will find spaces
for the ticket holder's

03:29.757 --> 03:31.967
name and telephone number…

03:34.262 --> 03:38.762
ICHIRO MORISHITA

03:35.597 --> 03:37.140
Ichiro Morishita…

03:38.391 --> 03:40.998
The name written here
doesn't match any of yours.

03:44.230 --> 03:45.689
N-Name?!

03:45.773 --> 03:47.441
Phone number?!

03:47.525 --> 03:50.069
That was written on the back?!

03:52.113 --> 03:53.489
E-Er…

03:53.573 --> 03:57.243
Well, well, well, well,
this is peculiar.

03:58.620 --> 04:02.040
This is your lottery ticket,
isn't it?

04:02.123 --> 04:04.208
Oh, yeah! Now I remember!

04:04.334 --> 04:08.713
I used it to write down
my friend's number!

04:08.796 --> 04:11.298
Oh! Is that so?

04:11.382 --> 04:15.882
Then whaddya say we give
Mr. Ichiro Morishita a call?

04:18.681 --> 04:22.226
All lottery tickets are traceable
to their point of purchase

04:22.310 --> 04:24.937
with their serial numbers.

04:25.480 --> 04:29.275
If Mr. Ichiro Morishita
indeed purchased a lottery ticket

04:29.567 --> 04:33.654
and can remember precisely
where he bought it,

04:34.072 --> 04:38.159
we will then be obliged
to confirm his signature…

04:40.328 --> 04:42.913
My, to whom does
this mysterious ticket belong?

04:45.667 --> 04:47.418
Depending on what we learn,

04:47.502 --> 04:49.462
we may have to
turn it over to the police.

04:50.004 --> 04:51.797
The police?!

04:52.757 --> 04:55.259
<i>Hello? Morishita speaking.</i>

04:55.552 --> 04:58.179
Hello, this is Budogaoka Bank.

04:58.388 --> 05:00.598
And I'm calling to inquire whether
a Mr. Ichiro Morishita

05:00.682 --> 05:04.977
purchased a Great Year-End
Lottery ticket.

05:05.436 --> 05:09.064
<i>Yeah, I'm Ichiro Morishita.
I bought one.</i>

05:12.277 --> 05:13.945
<i>In fact, I'm sure I bought one.</i>

05:16.739 --> 05:19.742
<i>Yes! I got you, you pathetic brats!</i>

05:19.826 --> 05:22.203
<i>I knew it, I still got it!</i>

05:22.453 --> 05:25.372
<i>As if god in heaven would
bestow the winning ticket</i>

05:25.456 --> 05:28.167
<i>on money-grubbing goons like you!</i>

05:33.548 --> 05:35.091
MORI

05:35.091 --> 05:38.260
So you did!
You bought a lottery ticket.

05:38.553 --> 05:40.512
<i>Yeah, I did.</i>

05:39.053 --> 05:42.222
MORISHITA ICHIRO

05:40.597 --> 05:45.601
<i>I must've bought ten of 'em,
but they were all duds.</i>

05:42.307 --> 05:45.601
KINOSHITA ICHIRO

05:46.394 --> 05:48.104
I'm returning only portions
of his writing

05:48.187 --> 05:49.438
to their original forms…

05:52.734 --> 05:54.986
Well I'm pleased to inform you,
Mr. Kinoshita,

05:55.069 --> 05:56.612
your lottery ticket…

05:56.779 --> 05:59.573
<i>Kinoshita? My name's Morishita.</i>

06:01.034 --> 06:02.994
Huh? But it was
the character for "Mori"!

06:03.077 --> 06:05.162
What? I just don't get it…

06:06.122 --> 06:10.622
Your phone number is 1771 -1281,
correct, Mr. Kinoshita?

06:11.878 --> 06:14.463
<i>I told you, pinhead,
my name's not Kinoshita!</i>

06:14.547 --> 06:15.589
<i>It's Morishita!</i>

06:15.673 --> 06:18.509
<i>Why're you wasting
my time with this baloney?</i>

06:18.593 --> 06:20.261
<i>I threw those damn things away</i>

06:20.386 --> 06:22.388
<i>Sell me a goddammed winner
next time…</i>

06:22.513 --> 06:24.848
I'm sorry for the inconvenience…

06:25.683 --> 06:28.477
Wait right there, boys!

06:28.978 --> 06:32.022
<i>The number you have reached
is no longer in service.</i>

06:32.398 --> 06:34.733
<i>Please check the number
and dial again…</i>

06:34.817 --> 06:37.236
That good enough?

06:37.737 --> 06:41.323
Please accept my deepest apologies.

06:43.284 --> 06:46.453
Yay! I got my money!

06:46.621 --> 06:49.540
My hard-won five million yen!

06:50.958 --> 06:55.458
Hey, you promised.
Half would go to us, Shigechi!

06:59.759 --> 07:01.844
Did I say that?

07:02.720 --> 07:04.513
You're pulling that shit again?!

07:05.682 --> 07:07.975
Hey, Josuke! What are you doing?!

07:08.476 --> 07:11.729
You're not gonna let him
get away with it again, are you?

07:11.813 --> 07:14.148
No… He's not getting off
scot-free this time!

07:15.149 --> 07:17.317
No more Mr. Nice guy!

07:18.611 --> 07:20.404
That's the spirit, Josuke!

07:20.488 --> 07:22.364
I knew you wouldn't back down!

07:22.573 --> 07:24.825
Who in their right mind would?!

07:25.451 --> 07:28.829
Not in the mood to split the money
three ways anymore, eh, Shigechi?

07:29.330 --> 07:32.541
That's just not gonna fly,
not with that kind of money.

07:37.463 --> 07:38.380
Here.

07:38.756 --> 07:41.216
This should be plenty for you guys.

07:41.968 --> 07:44.637
It's not like you guys
did anything.

07:45.096 --> 07:48.682
Think of that as a little
pity payment from your friend.

07:48.850 --> 07:49.976
CRUSH

07:51.310 --> 07:52.185
Why, you—

07:52.270 --> 07:53.354
Hey, Okuyasu!

07:53.479 --> 07:55.647
Hand it over, jerk-off!

07:55.732 --> 07:59.777
You promised us half,
and half is what we're gonna get!

07:59.902 --> 08:01.737
Serves you right, greedy bastard!

08:01.863 --> 08:05.199
You always let your fists
do the talking. Control yourself.

08:05.283 --> 08:06.909
When words don't work,

08:06.993 --> 08:09.245
a little manhandling
always does the trick!

08:10.705 --> 08:12.206
Are you hurt?

08:12.707 --> 08:15.751
Okuyasu shouldn't have hit you.

08:15.960 --> 08:19.088
Shigechi,
let's do this the easy way.

08:19.297 --> 08:21.841
We're gonna hold onto
the promissory note

08:21.924 --> 08:23.884
for the five million.

08:24.635 --> 08:26.762
When we cash it in three days,

08:27.221 --> 08:30.766
we'll split it, as promised,
half and half.

08:33.644 --> 08:36.229
I'm so over that asshole.

08:36.606 --> 08:39.650
No way in hell
I'm hanging with him anymore.

08:39.734 --> 08:40.735
But you know,

08:41.110 --> 08:44.863
we were the ones trying to exploit
the poor bastard for pocket money.

08:44.989 --> 08:47.282
Guess we have a lot
to be sorry about.

08:47.742 --> 08:48.534
You moron.

08:48.618 --> 08:49.452
Huh?

08:49.744 --> 08:52.580
Well, I see things
in a different way.

08:52.663 --> 08:56.792
He got his hands on that
five million only because of us.

08:57.001 --> 08:59.920
He'd be lucky to get
a few tens of thousands on his own.

09:00.004 --> 09:03.382
He's walking away with 2.5 million.

09:05.968 --> 09:08.220
2.5 million!

09:10.056 --> 09:12.850
Yes, yes, yes, yes,
yes, yes, yes, yes,

09:12.934 --> 09:14.727
yes, yes, yes, yes!

09:14.811 --> 09:16.646
It stays with me.

09:17.605 --> 09:20.107
It stays with me!

09:23.945 --> 09:27.031
I heard everything, sneaky bastard!

09:27.114 --> 09:30.534
I won't give you guys a single yen!

09:30.701 --> 09:35.080
We got that five million
because of Harvest!

09:35.373 --> 09:39.210
You're nothing compared
to my Harvest!

09:39.335 --> 09:40.753
Wanna see proof?

09:41.462 --> 09:43.755
You wanna see some hard proof?

09:45.550 --> 09:46.551
I'll show you!

09:47.385 --> 09:48.469
Ow!

09:50.471 --> 09:53.599
- Bastard!
- No! Our five million yen IOU!

09:53.850 --> 09:57.603
You're playing with
the wrong Stand users, dipshit!

09:58.479 --> 10:00.981
Keep chasing me,

10:01.732 --> 10:03.233
and I'll kill you.

10:05.152 --> 10:06.570
Shigechi…

10:06.654 --> 10:09.698
This fool says he's gonna kill us.

10:09.824 --> 10:14.324
If you sic your Stand on us,
then prepare to meet your maker!

10:16.622 --> 10:18.332
W-Wait, Josuke…

10:18.583 --> 10:19.542
What's wrong?

10:19.667 --> 10:21.794
I've got this weird feeling…

10:24.005 --> 10:25.381
M-My legs…

10:25.464 --> 10:27.799
they itch like a son of a bitch…

10:27.884 --> 10:30.344
Itch? At a time like this?

10:30.469 --> 10:33.013
It itches so bad!

10:33.097 --> 10:35.099
My whole body itches!

10:36.309 --> 10:38.602
Wh-What the hell is happening?!

10:38.686 --> 10:41.772
Roll up your pants, Okuyasu! Hurry!

10:41.856 --> 10:43.357
What?!

10:46.736 --> 10:49.739
They got inside my pants!

10:57.246 --> 10:58.538
I-It's no use!

10:58.623 --> 11:02.209
Knocking off two or three of 'em
won't hurt him at all!

11:02.335 --> 11:03.586
Dammit!

11:04.170 --> 11:06.088
He's getting away!

11:06.923 --> 11:08.549
He's starting to
really piss me off.

11:08.633 --> 11:11.719
This guy has been pissing me off
the whole time!

11:12.303 --> 11:14.263
Come to papa, five million!

11:14.430 --> 11:16.014
He just made mortal enemies

11:16.098 --> 11:20.018
of the hard-as-nails
Okuyasu-Josuke fighting duo!

11:23.814 --> 11:26.525
JOSUKE HIGASHIKATA

11:32.365 --> 11:35.785
Damn him!
No one makes a fool out of Okuyasu!

11:35.910 --> 11:37.411
I'll beat you into a bloody pulp!

11:37.536 --> 11:39.538
Well, now we know
he's a greedy bastard

11:39.622 --> 11:41.290
and a complete idiot.

11:41.582 --> 11:42.958
Blasted butterball!

11:43.042 --> 11:46.920
I'd think twice about
trying to outrun us with that body!

11:47.755 --> 11:50.174
See, told ya so, dumb-ass!

11:55.763 --> 12:00.263
H-He's using Harvest underneath him
like a tank's caterpillar track,

12:01.310 --> 12:03.186
or some kind of bucket relay!

12:03.270 --> 12:06.982
Shit… This guy's insane fast!

12:17.368 --> 12:18.952
He's not the brightest bulb
in the box,

12:19.036 --> 12:20.579
but he's actually kinda clever.

12:20.663 --> 12:22.665
It's like he comes up with
this crap by instinct.

12:23.749 --> 12:25.292
Damn! We lost him!

12:25.376 --> 12:26.835
Just hold your horses.

12:26.961 --> 12:28.253
All we gotta do is…

12:29.213 --> 12:30.339
pull the same trick

12:30.423 --> 12:34.593
and have our Stands
do all the heavy lifting!

12:35.678 --> 12:37.513
I get it!

12:42.309 --> 12:44.644
My five million…

12:46.230 --> 12:49.358
You really think you can
get away from us, Shigechi?

12:50.776 --> 12:51.902
Bring it, blimp!

12:51.986 --> 12:56.486
I'm gonna pop each and every one
of your little Harvest underlings!

13:01.454 --> 13:03.706
My Harvest is amazing.

13:03.831 --> 13:05.999
It can collect anything!

13:09.211 --> 13:11.880
Even the kind of screws
that hold pipes together.

13:11.964 --> 13:13.382
Bolts too!

13:17.553 --> 13:19.012
I think you're forgetting about

13:19.096 --> 13:21.598
the amazingness of
my Shining Diamond!

13:30.483 --> 13:31.775
Well, hello.

13:34.528 --> 13:37.072
I'm madder than hell,

13:37.156 --> 13:39.575
but I'm still willing
to forgive you.

13:39.784 --> 13:42.578
As long as I get
a few good last hits in!

13:42.703 --> 13:46.248
Come on, give us that IOU,
Shigechi.

13:46.874 --> 13:48.959
I told you…

13:49.043 --> 13:50.627
Keep chasing me,

13:51.796 --> 13:53.005
and I'll kill you.

13:56.217 --> 13:58.302
W-What?

13:58.719 --> 13:59.720
My hands…

14:03.307 --> 14:04.558
That hurt…

14:05.976 --> 14:09.604
I can't get up! Okuyasu, watch out!

14:09.980 --> 14:11.690
He's up to something!

14:13.192 --> 14:15.110
O-Okuyasu, you too?

14:16.570 --> 14:18.780
Still can't figure it out?

14:18.864 --> 14:22.075
You guys are drunk!

14:22.159 --> 14:23.869
A-Alcohol?!

14:24.078 --> 14:26.038
LIQUOR

14:24.370 --> 14:26.059
My harvest can get their hands
on anything!

14:28.207 --> 14:31.960
It carried some booze
all the way from the liquor store,

14:32.086 --> 14:36.298
then injected it into your bodies!

14:36.882 --> 14:39.968
Directly into your veins, in fact!

14:40.094 --> 14:41.553
W-What?!

14:44.932 --> 14:46.433
You bastard!

14:46.851 --> 14:49.144
When alcohol's injected
into the veins,

14:49.228 --> 14:52.272
it doesn't take much
to get shit-faced!

14:52.523 --> 14:53.774
C-Come to think of it,

14:53.983 --> 14:58.483
alcohol can be used as
an anesthetic…

14:59.446 --> 15:00.905
Th-That bastard…

15:00.990 --> 15:02.992
He isn't a total idiot,
after all…

15:03.284 --> 15:05.160
No, it must be instinct.

15:05.619 --> 15:07.996
I-I'm gonna murder him!

15:08.080 --> 15:12.580
No way is a little tipsiness
gonna bring me down!

15:18.924 --> 15:20.175
M-My eye!

15:20.301 --> 15:23.220
Josuke, hurry, fix it quick!

15:23.429 --> 15:24.930
W-Wait, Okuyasu!

15:25.264 --> 15:27.641
If I remember correctly,

15:27.725 --> 15:29.101
you guys called me unreasonable

15:29.185 --> 15:31.520
and a whole bunch of other things,
didn't you?

15:31.812 --> 15:36.312
I'll show you what happens
when you underestimate me!

15:37.318 --> 15:38.861
D-Damn it!

15:39.320 --> 15:43.782
So I guess that means you forgot
all about breaking your promise?

15:43.866 --> 15:45.951
That's it… I'm this close!

15:46.076 --> 15:48.411
Push me more, and I can't
guarantee what'll happen!

15:49.455 --> 15:52.583
That's enough lip out of you,
Josuke!

15:52.917 --> 15:56.712
You've got a sad excuse of a Stand!

15:56.795 --> 15:58.713
You guys's powers are shit!

15:58.839 --> 16:03.339
Try making demands after
you've got half of Harvest's power!

16:03.636 --> 16:05.262
Josuke, close your eyes!

16:07.264 --> 16:08.598
Josuke!

16:08.682 --> 16:10.058
So close!

16:10.309 --> 16:13.228
There's no point
in closing your eyes.

16:13.354 --> 16:15.898
Harvest can get anything!

16:16.023 --> 16:20.523
He'll just tear off your eyelid
and gorge out your eye!

16:23.030 --> 16:25.282
We get it, Shigechi, stop!

16:25.407 --> 16:29.035
Forgive us! We were wrong.

16:29.119 --> 16:30.912
Oh? Is that an apology?

16:31.121 --> 16:33.998
Damn it, you little punk!

16:34.166 --> 16:38.295
Oh? Okuyasu, it seems Josuke
doesn't share your sentiment.

16:38.379 --> 16:40.547
I-I'll make him share my sentiment!

16:41.257 --> 16:43.050
We'll give you this!

16:44.426 --> 16:48.513
It's the 10,000 yen you gave me
and everything else I have.

16:48.597 --> 16:51.266
Take it as our penitence.

16:51.433 --> 16:55.933
Who's gonna fix my eye
if Josuke is offed?

16:56.272 --> 16:57.815
O-Okuyasu…

17:00.025 --> 17:03.278
Oh, yeah! That's right!

17:03.404 --> 17:07.904
I felt so bad for you guys,
I blessed you with over 10,000 yen!

17:09.243 --> 17:13.247
Here, take it,
just have mercy on us.

17:19.003 --> 17:20.629
<i>Brilliant, Okuyasu!</i>

17:20.754 --> 17:24.048
<i>Like catching a tanuki
with a little bait,</i>

17:24.133 --> 17:27.594
<i>you'll lure him in
with some cash and then bam!</i>

17:28.095 --> 17:32.224
<i>I'm right there with you, buddy!</i>

17:32.516 --> 17:37.016
Okuyasu, that newfound obedience
leaves a good impression.

17:37.730 --> 17:38.897
There, there.

17:44.278 --> 17:46.154
Hey, wait a sec.

17:46.447 --> 17:50.826
Okuyasu, you wouldn't be trying to
lure me in with cash

17:50.909 --> 17:53.995
so you can attack me
with your Stand, would you?

17:55.122 --> 17:57.457
Ah! So you are!

17:58.625 --> 18:03.125
Did you really think
I'd fall for that?

18:03.255 --> 18:05.674
You really thought
I was that stupid?

18:06.842 --> 18:08.134
No more pity!

18:08.427 --> 18:10.679
Fine by us,
we don't need your pity.

18:11.138 --> 18:13.223
But it's too late.

18:13.307 --> 18:17.807
Didn't realize you're already
well within The Hand's range?

18:20.439 --> 18:22.649
I'll claw away mid-air

18:23.150 --> 18:24.734
and make it

18:24.860 --> 18:25.902
teleport!

18:25.986 --> 18:27.570
We got back what's rightfully ours.

18:27.654 --> 18:29.364
Got it back?

18:29.448 --> 18:31.366
W-What are you talking about?

18:33.160 --> 18:35.453
I'll just take it back…

18:35.537 --> 18:38.122
You just don't get it,
do you, Shigechi?

18:38.248 --> 18:41.709
Your chance of winning
just expired.

18:41.794 --> 18:42.920
My five million!

18:43.003 --> 18:45.005
What are you doing?!

18:45.089 --> 18:46.590
I don't get it! I don't get it!

18:46.715 --> 18:48.258
Stop!

18:48.467 --> 18:51.386
Why would you do that?!

18:51.512 --> 18:54.681
I don't get it! I don't get it!
I don't get it! I don't get it!

18:54.765 --> 18:56.057
That's five million yen!

18:56.183 --> 19:00.353
You could try to hurt us…
even kill us.

19:00.604 --> 19:02.063
But, you see,
the only way of fixing this thing

19:02.147 --> 19:04.774
is with Shining Diamond…

19:05.317 --> 19:07.485
You can't win this fight.

19:07.611 --> 19:10.572
Oh… I-I see! I get it!

19:10.656 --> 19:14.534
And with this, you can
kiss any hope of victory good bye.

19:14.618 --> 19:17.287
H-Huh? I don't get it!
I don't get it!

19:17.371 --> 19:18.914
I don't get it! I don't get it!

19:19.039 --> 19:20.790
What are you doing?!

19:20.916 --> 19:24.419
Get every last scrap, Harvest!

19:26.755 --> 19:28.631
Guess I gotta spell it out
for you again…

19:29.341 --> 19:33.720
Sending Harvest after the pieces
was the nail in the coffin.

19:35.556 --> 19:40.056
So who's gonna protect you
from these two drunks now?

19:42.396 --> 19:44.272
Oh, I get it…

19:44.898 --> 19:46.107
SMASH

19:49.194 --> 19:51.029
We did it.

19:51.155 --> 19:53.907
So, old buddy, old pal…

19:53.991 --> 19:57.160
I think we're due for
a little study time.

19:57.244 --> 20:00.789
The little scraps are
picked up by Harvest, and…

20:01.039 --> 20:03.833
the little scraps are
put back together by…?

20:04.585 --> 20:05.335
Well?

20:05.419 --> 20:06.503
I'm waiting…

20:06.795 --> 20:09.881
Who can put the scraps
back together with Shining Diamond?

20:10.048 --> 20:11.424
J-Josuke…

20:11.592 --> 20:14.469
WHACK
WHACK

20:14.636 --> 20:16.346
M-Mr. Josuke, sir!

20:16.430 --> 20:18.473
Damn straight, Mr. Josuke, sir.

20:18.765 --> 20:22.435
And the one who recovered
that IOU from you is…

20:22.936 --> 20:24.687
Say his name.

20:25.063 --> 20:26.189
O-Okuyasu…

20:26.773 --> 20:27.648
Mr. Okuyasu!

20:27.941 --> 20:29.692
That's it. Good boy.

20:30.068 --> 20:33.154
All right,
it's time for mathematics.

20:33.447 --> 20:35.991
How do we split the five million?

20:36.492 --> 20:39.495
How do we split it
so that everyone is happy?

20:40.704 --> 20:42.247
I'm happy with half…

20:42.331 --> 20:43.623
Half?

20:43.790 --> 20:46.793
You do know there are
three of us here, right?

20:46.877 --> 20:49.546
Half doesn't seem at all
weird to you?

20:49.755 --> 20:53.008
That's just not very good math.

20:54.593 --> 20:56.219
Anyone home?

20:58.388 --> 21:01.140
I-It'd be a third…

21:03.477 --> 21:05.395
Th-That's right…

21:05.479 --> 21:08.273
I'd have only been able
to gather stuff.

21:08.649 --> 21:10.859
I-I was wrong.

21:11.318 --> 21:14.195
We all found this lottery ticket.

21:14.655 --> 21:16.114
We wouldn't have ever gotten it

21:16.198 --> 21:17.699
without the three of us
working together.

21:17.824 --> 21:18.699
I…

21:19.201 --> 21:20.994
I can see now.

21:21.495 --> 21:24.331
My greed kept me
from seeing the truth.

21:24.665 --> 21:27.542
We split everything fair and square
so everyone is happy.

21:29.670 --> 21:31.046
BAM

21:31.296 --> 21:32.213
Yes!

21:32.631 --> 21:33.840
Real cash!

21:34.007 --> 21:35.633
I-It's five million yen!

21:35.759 --> 21:40.259
Rest assured your money
would be safe with Budogaoka Bank.

21:41.723 --> 21:42.432
Of course!

21:42.516 --> 21:45.477
We finally did it!
I must be dreaming!

21:45.686 --> 21:46.978
Wait…

21:47.104 --> 21:49.106
Weren't we gonna
split everything up

21:49.189 --> 21:50.565
so everyone would be happy?

21:50.941 --> 21:53.234
Huh? That's strange.

21:53.360 --> 21:55.612
If we're gonna split it up
fair and square,

21:55.862 --> 21:58.823
don't we have to
include our Stands?

21:59.116 --> 22:03.078
Harvest is made up of
about 500 Stands,

22:03.245 --> 22:07.745
so we should split it
500 to 1 and 1.

22:08.667 --> 22:10.960
You don't disagree, do you?

22:11.044 --> 22:12.295
You little bastard!

22:12.421 --> 22:13.839
Trying to haggle again?

22:13.922 --> 22:16.466
You still don't know
when to stop, do you, idiot!

22:16.550 --> 22:19.135
Okay, one third is fine!

22:19.303 --> 22:23.803
JOSUKE HIGASHIKATA
- CURRENT SAVINGS - 1,666,666 YEN

22:20.220 --> 22:22.013
<i>For some, that is far too much</i>

22:22.097 --> 22:24.557
<i>for a high school freshman
to have, but…</i>

22:25.017 --> 22:25.121
<i>To be continued!</i>

23:38.882 --> 23:42.010
EPISODE 20
YUKAKO YAMAGISHI
DREAMS OF CINDERELLA
